Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Brume renders pages with the Microsoft Edge WebView2 runtime, which is not
redistributed here and remains subject to its own terms.

The Rust dependency tree is predominantly Apache-2.0 or MIT. It also includes
components under the Mozilla Public License 2.0, currently adblock, cssparser,
cssparser-macros, dtoa-short, option-ext and selectors. MPL-2.0 is file-level
copyleft: those files stay under MPL-2.0 and their source is available from
crates.io. None of them are modified here.

adblock is listed first because it is a deliberate choice rather than something
that arrived underneath another crate. It is Brave's content blocking engine,
from https://github.com/brave/adblock-rust/, and it is what Brume matches filter
rules with.

Brume does not redistribute any filter list. EasyList and the lists derived from
it are CC BY-SA 3.0, and bundling one would mean carrying that licence and its
share-alike terms into this repository. They are downloaded on the user's own
machine, from the publishers, and cached there. What ships here is the engine,
not the rules.

Archivo is bundled under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. See
brand/assets/fonts/README.md.

The UI icon set is Lucide, redistributed under the ISC License. Every file in
brand/assets/icons/ carries the notice, except cleave.svg, which is Brume's own
mark and no part of Lucide.

Some of the icons Brume uses are derived from the Feather project and are MIT
rather than ISC. Of the set bundled here that covers arrow-left, arrow-right,
check, chevron-down, chevron-right, download, external-link, info, lock,
maximize, minimize, minus, plus, search, sidebar, square, trash-2, upload, x,
zoom-in and zoom-out. Both notices follow, as shipped by Lucide.

